{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"b4bbuegfm","tool_use_id":"toolu_01N9KgQrTFRK6oL5FVuWKMqj","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-441489/-scratch-users-kushinm-auto-psych-outer-loop-live-runs-run2-repo/8f54b17c-fa34-4aae-9717-d0a890cb62c8/tasks/b4bbuegfm.output","summary":"Background command \"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4_repair_1\necho triplet_variety_balanced_alternation_ideal > $D/model_name.txt\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `balance_aware_heads_alternation_ideal`: people still judge a sequence by how close its switching rate is to their own ideal (person-specific, length-scaled sensitivity, shared penalty for periodic sequences), still favour heads-leaning sequences and still find lopsided H/T counts less random — but they also register the variety of short local patterns, so a sequence whose overlapping three-flip chunks are mostly different from one another (rather than the same few chunks recurring) looks more random, even when its overall switching rate is the same. The one change is a shared reward on the share of distinct three-flip chunks a sequence contains, addressing the critique (surviving FDR, q = 0.008) that among pairs with equal switch counts people pick the sequence with more distinct triplets far more often than the incumbent predicts.\nEOF\npython3 - << 'PY'\nsrc = open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/models/balance_aware_heads_alternation_ideal.py\").read()\ndoc_old = src[:src.index('import numpy')]\ndoc_new = '''\"\"\"Triplet-variety balanced heads-default alternation ideal.\n\nRefinement of `balance_aware_heads_alternation_ideal`: people judge a sequence\nby how close its switching rate is to their own ideal (person-specific,\nlength-scaled sensitivity; shared periodicity penalty), favour heads-leaning\nsequences and dislike lopsided H/T counts, and they also register the variety\nof short local patterns: a sequence whose overlapping three-flip chunks are\nmostly distinct looks more random than one that reuses the same few chunks,\nat the same switching rate. The one change is the shared triplet-variety\nweight `rho`.\n\"\"\"\n'''\nsrc = src.replace(doc_old, doc_new)\nsrc = src.replace('''    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''', '''    def triplet_variety(seq):\n        # Share of the possible distinct three-flip chunks the sequence shows.\n        n_windows = len(seq) - 2\n        if n_windows <= 0:\n            return 0.0\n        distinct = len({seq[i:i + 3] for i in range(n_windows)})\n        return distinct / min(8, n_windows)\n\n    a = sequence_a.strip().upper()''')\nsrc = src.replace('''        \"log_trans\":''', '''        # Triplet variety, a minus b (positive favours a).\n        \"triplet_variety_diff\": triplet_variety(a) - triplet_variety(b),\n        \"log_trans\":''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    log_trans = pm.Data(''', '''    trip_diff = pm.Data(\"triplet_variety_diff\", np.zeros(1, dtype=\"float64\"))\n    log_trans = pm.Data(''')\nsrc = src.replace('''    theta = ideal''', '''    # Reward for local pattern variety (positive: more distinct triplets look\n    # more random).\n    rho = pm.Normal(\"rho\", mu=0.0, sigma=2.0)\n\n    theta = ideal''')\nsrc = src.replace('''        + eta * imb_diff\n''', '''        + eta * imb_diff\n        + rho * trip_diff\n''')\nopen(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4_repair_1/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nPY\ngrep -n \"rho\\|trip\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run2/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run2/data/subjective_randomness/experiment2/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5\" completed (exit code 0)","uuid":"a4ceed39-31a6-4e59-ad4d-47dadfd755e1","session_id":"8f54b17c-fa34-4aae-9717-d0a890cb62c8"}
